GCC commands
commands                                   Description
gcc filename.c                             Compiles filename.c and creates an executable file named a.out
gcc -o output filename.c	                 Compiles filename.c and creates an executable file named output.
gcc -c filename.c	                         Compiles filename.c into an object file (filename.o) without linking.
gcc -Wall filename.c	                     Enables all warning messages during compilation.
gcc -g filename.c	                         Compiles with debug information included (required for debugging with GDB).
gcc -O	                                   Optimizes the code (basic optimization).
gcc -O1, -O2, -O3	                         Compiles with increasing levels of optimization (higher numbers = more aggressive optimization).
gcc -std=c99 filename.c	                   Compiles with the C99 standard.
gcc -ansi filename.c	                     Enforces strict ANSI C compliance.
gcc -E filename.c	                         Runs only the preprocessor and outputs preprocessed code.
gcc -S filename.c	                         Generates assembly code (.s file) from the source code.
gcc -L/path/to/libs	                       Adds a directory to the library search path during linking.
gcc -l<libname>	                           Links the program to a library named lib<libname>.so or lib<libname>.a.
gcc -I/path/to/include	                   Specifies an additional directory to search for header files.
gcc -pthread filename.c	                   Compiles and links a program with the pthread (POSIX thread) library.
gcc -shared -fPIC filename.c	             Compiles and creates a shared library.
gcc -D<macro>	                             Defines a macro during compilation (e.g., gcc -DDEBUG filename.c).
gcc -Werror	                               Treats all warnings as errors, stopping compilation if any warning occurs.
gcc -v	                                   Displays verbose output of the compilation process.
gcc --version	                             Displays the GCC version installed.

gcc -save-temps -o program program.c       Saves intermediate files for all compilation stages in the same directory as the source file.

GDB Commands
Starting and Exiting GDB
commands                       Description
gdb	                           Starts GDB.
gdb ./program	                 Starts GDB and loads the specified program.
gdb -q ./program	             Starts GDB in quiet mode (without the introductory message).
quit or q	                     Exits GDB.

Loading Files and Running Programs
commands                       Description
file ./program	               Loads an executable file into GDB.
run	                           Runs the program from the beginning.
run [args]	                   Runs the program with command-line arguments (e.g., run arg1 arg2).
start	                         Starts the program and pauses at the beginning of the main function.
set args	                     Sets command-line arguments for the program.

Breakpoints and Watchpoints
commands                       Description
break [location]	             Sets a breakpoint at a specific location (e.g., break main, break filename.c:line_number).
tbreak [location]	             Sets a temporary breakpoint (removes itself after being hit once).
info breakpoints	             Displays all breakpoints and their details.
delete [num]	                 Deletes a specific breakpoint (use delete to remove all breakpoints).
watch [variable]	             Sets a watchpoint to stop execution when the value of a variable changes.
rwatch [variable]	             Stops execution when the variable is read.
awatch [variable]	             Stops execution when the variable is read or written.

Controlling Program Execution
commands                       Description
continue or c	                 Resumes execution until the next breakpoint or program end.
step or s	                     Steps into the next line of code, including function calls.
next or n	                     Steps over the next line of code, skipping over function calls.
finish	                       Continues execution until the current function returns.
until [location]	             Runs the program until a specific location is reached.
return	                       Forces the current function to return immediately.
kill	                         Stops the program and terminates the debugging session.

Inspecting Program State
commands                       Description
print [expression]	           Prints the value of an expression (e.g., print x, print 5+3).
ptype [variable]	             Displays the data type of a variable.
display [expression]	         Automatically prints the value of an expression after every step.
info locals	                   Lists all local variables in the current function and their values.
info registers	               Displays the values of CPU registers.
info stack	                   Shows the current call stack.
backtrace or bt	               Displays the call stack (useful for identifying where a crash occurred).
frame [num]	                   Switches to a specific stack frame.
list	                         Displays source code near the current execution point.
list [location]	               Displays source code around a specified location (e.g., list main).

Memory and Variables
commands                       Description
x [address]	                   Examines memory at a given address (e.g., x/4xw 0x600ff0).
set [variable] = value	       Changes the value of a variable during runtime.
info variables	               Displays all global and static variables.

Advanced Debugging
commands                       Description
set follow-fork-mode	         Sets how GDB handles forked processes (e.g., child, parent).
attach [pid]	                 Attaches GDB to a running process using its PID.
detach	                       Detaches GDB from the current process.
info sharedlibrary	           Displays shared libraries loaded by the program.

Miscellaneous
commands                       Description
help	                         Lists all GDB commands or provides help on a specific command.
show [option]	                 Displays the current value of a GDB setting (e.g., show args).
set pagination off	           Disables pagination of output in GDB.
